WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.203 --> 00:00:13.783
was a dark, starless night.

2
00:00:14.544 --> 00:00:16.504
The moon was hidden in the cloudy sky.

3
00:00:17.804 --> 00:00:21.626
Peter crawled on his belly, snake-like, across the ground.

4
00:00:22.866 --> 00:00:25.847
This was one of many useful things the Indians had taught him.

5
00:00:26.987 --> 00:00:32.453
Tinker Bell was still too weak to fly and light the way, so Peter had decided not to

6
00:00:32.513 --> 00:00:33.273
fly himself.

7
00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:38.996
He knew where he was headed—the pirate ship, the Jolly Roger!

8
00:00:40.236 --> 00:00:45.438
Suddenly, Peter caught sight of the crocodile, which was also creeping in the dark.

9
00:00:46.639 --> 00:00:50.540
No other living creature seemed to be awake but the boy and the crocodile.

10
00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:55.322
And they were both after the same prey—Captain Hook.

11
00:00:57.363 --> 00:01:01.917
In the silence of the night, Peter realized something was different about the crocodile.

12
00:01:03.057 --> 00:01:05.798
The clock inside it had finally stopped ticking.

13
00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:09.499
At that moment, Peter had an idea.

14
00:01:10.639 --> 00:01:16.501
He was determined to rescue Wendy and the boys, but he was also eager to destroy his rival.

15
00:01:16.521 --> 00:01:20.122
"This time, it's Hook or me!"

16
00:01:20.842 --> 00:01:22.883
he thought with great excitement.

17
00:01:24.023 --> 00:01:25.744
And he started to form a plan.

18
00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:30.530
The Jolly Roger was anchored not far from the shore of Kidd's Creek.

19
00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:37.434
On board, some of the pirates were sleeping, and others were playing dice and cards.

20
00:01:39.115 --> 00:01:46.319
Even though it was after midnight, Smee sat at the ship's sewing machine, busily mending the captain's clothes.

21
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.781
Hook walked the deck deep in thought.

22
00:01:50.962 --> 00:01:53.163
This should have been his moment of triumph.

23
00:01:53.803 --> 00:01:54.664
Peter was dead.

24
00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:58.182
The boys were tied up and soon would walk the plank.

25
00:01:59.282 --> 00:02:00.743
And Wendy was his captive.

26
00:02:01.263 --> 00:02:03.465
But Hook felt unhappy and alone.

27
00:02:05.006 --> 00:02:07.667
Even among his pirates, Hook was lonely.

28
00:02:08.668 --> 00:02:11.089
They were no better than dogs that obeyed him.

29
00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.772
They certainly were not equals who could listen to his feelings.

30
00:02:16.993 --> 00:02:19.454
How cruel fate had been to the captain!

31
00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:22.176
Hook hadn't always been a pirate.

32
00:02:24.704 --> 00:02:26.325
Hook wasn't even his real name.

33
00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:30.828
Once, he had been a promising young man at a private school.

34
00:02:31.908 --> 00:02:36.471
There he had learned the manners and fancy dress that could have made him a gentleman.

35
00:02:37.691 --> 00:02:41.493
But he had wanted fame, and evil had taken hold of him.

36
00:02:41.513 --> 00:02:45.656
"What good are all my evil triumphs in the end?

37
00:02:46.336 --> 00:02:49.078
No little children love me," he thought.

38
00:02:50.258 --> 00:02:52.920
It was strange that he should suddenly think of these things.

39
00:02:54.056 --> 00:02:56.277
Maybe it was the sound of Smee's sewing machine.

40
00:02:58.597 --> 00:03:01.978
Even though he was a pirate, old Smee was lovable.

41
00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:06.700
There was not a child on board the ship who did not already love Smee.

42
00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:13.882
He had given Wendy a cloak to keep warm, and Michael had even tried on his glasses.

43
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:20.064
does Smee have that I do not?"

44
00:03:20.724 --> 00:03:21.444
wondered Hook.

45
00:03:22.572 --> 00:03:25.494
He needed to do something wicked to feel better again.

46
00:03:26.794 --> 00:03:33.837
Standing a little taller, Hook shouted to his men, "Are all the boys chained so they cannot fly

47
00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:37.219
away?" "Ay, ay," they answered.

48
00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:41.381
"Then bring them up," he ordered.

49
00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:45.362
The poor prisoners were dragged from the hold below.

50
00:03:46.403 --> 00:03:48.684
The eight boys stood in a line in front of him.

51
00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.977
"Six of you will walk the plank tonight.

52
00:03:52.857 --> 00:03:55.698
But I will keep two to be my cabin boys.

53
00:03:56.699 --> 00:03:58.320
Who wishes to serve me?"

54
00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.421
The boys were silent.

55
00:04:02.281 --> 00:04:04.062
Finally Tootles spoke up.

56
00:04:04.082 --> 00:04:09.344
"Sir, I don't think my mother would like me to be a pirate.

57
00:04:10.425 --> 00:04:13.026
Would your mother like you to be a pirate, Slightly?"

58
00:04:13.046 --> 00:04:20.553
"I don't think so," Slightly answered sadly, as if he wished it were otherwise.

59
00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:22.995
The other boys agreed.

60
00:04:24.556 --> 00:04:25.997
Hook was angry.

61
00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:28.339
He looked directly at John.

62
00:04:28.359 --> 00:04:33.042
"You seem to have a little more courage, boy," he said.

63
00:04:33.062 --> 00:04:35.844
"Did you ever want to be a pirate?"

64
00:04:36.824 --> 00:04:38.185
John became thoughtful.

65
00:04:38.205 --> 00:04:42.608
"Yes, there was a time when I wanted to be a pirate."

66
00:04:43.489 --> 00:04:45.210
Then he looked around at his friends.

67
00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.332
"But that was long ago."

68
00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.781
"Then go to your doom!"

69
00:04:51.422 --> 00:04:52.182
Hook roared.

70
00:04:53.563 --> 00:04:56.986
To his men he said, "Get the plank ready!

71
00:04:57.346 --> 00:04:59.328
And bring up their mother to watch!"
